meta {
  name: Create Product Category
  type: http
  seq: 3
}

post {
  url: {{pim_base_url_v3}}/product-categories
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
  Content-Type: application/json
  Accept: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "name": "WC Test Category"
  }
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 201
  res.body.data.name: eq WC Test Category
}

docs {
  Confirmed live 2026-09-07 against "David's Dev Account". **Fixture kept**
  -- id `6a9f1b482b6fd055ffb7c7dc`, referenced by "Create Child Product
  Category.bru" in this folder and by Phase 2b (`02-Products-v3`) as a
  `category_ids` value once products are extended.

  ## Mutating status code confirmed
  `201 Created` -- matches `API V3.md`'s stated convention, **not**
  `openapi_pimv3.json`'s declared `200`/`422`-only responses. First
  confirmed mutating-status-code data point for `TESTING_PLAN.md`'s
  "don't assume" ground rule -- log per resource as each phase creates
  something.

  Create-response shape is a subset of the full `GET`-by-id shape (missing
  `account_id`, `parent_id`, `created` -- see "Get Product Category by
  ID.bru").

  ## Not idempotent to re-run
  Category names are unique per account. Re-running this exact request
  after the fixture already exists returns `422
  {"errors":[{"name":"ValidationError","description":"Category WC Test
  Category already exists"}]}` instead of `201` -- expected once the
  fixture is already in place, not a bug (see
  `config/api-testing.config.md` quirk #25a).
}
